          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: In September 1979, around 6:30 PM, a witness, alone outside their property, observes a bright object appearing on the horizon. This object moves very slowly in a north-south direction. Thinking it was a commercial airliner, the witness does not look away from the object. It comes to a stop above the witness, who then observes a very bright, metallic gray spherical object. After approximately one minute of being stationary, the object reverses direction, reaching the horizon in a few seconds and disappearing completely. No unusual noises were heard during the observation. This very late (October 2007) and poorly documented testimony does not allow for a serious investigation that could validate or refute certain hypotheses, such as an airliner making a turn, a balloon subject to wind shear, etc.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "616af3c012670af686f2dfb9429cd1c04607fc4ed1f566cd59f5f2f6d0a66b26"
